<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	@* viewport-fit=cover so the bottom nav bar's env(safe-area-inset-bottom) padding is a
	   real number on a notched phone. Without it the browser reports 0 and the icons sit
	   under the home indicator - the web build is used on phones too, not just desktops. *@
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
	<base href="/" />
	<ResourcePreloader />
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/BlazorDLR.Shared/lib/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" />
	@* Vendored, not a CDN: the nav is icons, and a rider out of signal must still be able
	   to read their own menu. Same reason Bootstrap sits next to it. *@
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/BlazorDLR.Shared/lib/fontawesome/css/all.min.css" />
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/BlazorDLR.Shared/app.css" />
	@*
		The scoped-component bundle. Named for the ASSEMBLY, not the project, and this
		one's assembly name is DLR.Server (.csproj) - the old `BlazorDLR.Web.styles.css`
		404'd, which is presumably why it ended up commented out. With it absent the web
		host rendered every .razor.css in the shared RCL as nothing at all: MainLayout and
		NavMenu had no rail layout, on the one host where you notice a window resize.
	*@
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="DLR.Server.styles.css" />
	<ImportMap />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="_content/BlazorDLR.Shared/favicon.png" />
	@* Publishes which edge the camera cutout is on as `data-notch`, because in landscape iOS
	   reports the same side inset on both edges and the nav rail only wants clearance on the
	   one that has a cutout. The web build is used on phones too. Not deferred: it has to
	   have run before the first paint, or the rail lands in the wrong place and slides. *@
	<script src="_content/BlazorDLR.Shared/safe-area.js"></script>
	<HeadOutlet @rendermode="@ClientRenderMode" />
</head>

<body>
	<Routes @rendermode="@ClientRenderMode" />

	<div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
		An unhandled error has occurred.
		<a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
		<span class="dismiss">🗙</span>
	</div>

	<script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>

@*
	Prerendering off. The one route the anonymous user is meant to land on is /welcome, and
	Home is [Authorize]-gated (§7.9). With prerendering on, the SSR pass rendered the gated
	Home, hit <NotAuthorized>, tried to Nav.NavigateTo("/welcome"), and the redirect thrown
	inside an interactive-mode boundary surfaced as the yellow error banner rather than as
	the redirect the browser needed. Auth state is a client-only concept on this host - the
	access token lives in the WASM heap (§7.4, §18.5), so there is nothing for the server to
	prerender authoritatively. Ship the WASM shell; let the client boot and resolve the route.
*@
@code {
	private static readonly InteractiveWebAssemblyRenderMode ClientRenderMode = new(prerender: false);
}
